      "name": "CleanupPauseCriticalSection",
      "signature": "undefined4 CleanupPauseCriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Cleans up and releases the pause rendering critical section.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_pcsPause global pointer\n2. If NULL, skip cleanup and return 1\n3. Call DeleteCriticalSection to release the critical section\n4. Queue a log message (params: g_pcsPause, 0x6f8992b4, 0, 0x63)\n5. Set g_pcsPause to NULL\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pcsPause is already NULL, function exits early returning 1\n  - Safe to call multiple times (idempotent cleanup)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - AcquirePauseRenderLock (0x6f8912e0) - Acquires the pause lock\n  - LeavePauseCriticalSection (0x6f891350) - Leaves without deleting\n\nGlobal References:\n  - g_pcsPause (0x6f89c874) - Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION for pause state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:48268a8384ed409dc561c8a7f58f70760e96135a889494351ff081c3c7adac1c",
