      "name": "InitializeDIBSection",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeDIBSection(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes a GDI Device Independent Bitmap (DIB) section for 2D rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1028-byte stack frame for BITMAPINFOHEADER and color table\n2. Save hdc parameter to global g_hGdiContext at 0x6f89bf2c\n3. Call internal helper function with nFlags parameter\n4. Initialize 256-entry color table (palette) with zeros\n5. Configure BITMAPINFOHEADER structure on stack:\n   - Set biWidth and biHeight dimensions\n   - Configure color depth and compression settings\n6. Call CreateDIBSection API to create device-independent bitmap\n7. Store returned DIB handle to global at 0x6f89bf30\n8. Call secondary initialization helper for palette setup\n9. Return TRUE (1) indicating successful initialization\n\nParameters:\n  hdc (ECX): Device context handle for GDI rendering operations\n  nFlags (EDX): Initialization flags controlling DIB creation behavior\n\nReturns:\n  int: 1 (TRUE) on successful DIB section creation, 0 on failure\n\nNote:\nFunction body appears malformed in Ghidra analysis (only first instruction visible).\nDocumentation derived from hex dump analysis of bytes at 0x6f8910b0-0x6f891117.",
