      "name": "GetBufferDimensions",
      "signature": "void GetBufferDimensions(int * pnWidth, int * pnHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Retrieves the current offscreen buffer dimensions (width and height).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read g_nTileProjectOffset (buffer width) into output pointer pnWidth\n2. Read g_nBufferHeight (buffer height) into output pointer pnHeight\n3. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pnWidth (ECX): Output pointer to receive buffer width in pixels\n  pnHeight (EDX): Output pointer to receive buffer height in pixels\n\nReturns: void\n\nNotes:\n  - Buffer dimensions are set by CreateOffscreenDIBSection based on resolution mode\n  - Possible values: 640x480, 800x600, or 1344x700\n  - g_nTileProjectOffset is misnamed; it actually stores buffer width",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
