      "name": "SetPaletteFromEntries",
      "signature": "undefined SetPaletteFromEntries(PALETTEENTRY * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Updates the system palette with the provided palette entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Convert palette entries from RGBX to BGRX format, storing in g_abConvertedPalette\n   - Loop iterates 256 times (0x100 entries, 4 bytes each = 0x400 bytes total)\n   - End address check: 0x6f89c46c + 0x400 = 0x6f89c86c\n2. Call Windows SetPaletteEntries to apply palette to g_hPalette handle\n3. Copy original palette entries to g_aPaletteCache (256 PALETTEENTRY structs)\n\nParameters:\n  pPaletteEntries (ECX) - Pointer to array of 256 PALETTEENTRY structures\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Assumes exactly 256 palette entries (standard 8-bit palette)\n  - Input palette is preserved unchanged; only converted copy stored\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x100 - Number of palette entries (256)\n  0x6f89c46c - Start of g_abConvertedPalette buffer\n  0x6f89c86c - End of converted palette buffer (start + 0x400)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:534f42058fe75ba9b7f320ecffe89ddc4cc5dee62e12ce3adad2b581fb249ba6",
