      "name": "ResetGdiRenderer",
      "signature": "undefined4 ResetGdiRenderer(undefined4 param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Resets and reinitializes the GDI renderer with a new resolution mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Delete existing GDI tile render bitmap object\n2. Clear frame buffer pointer to NULL\n3. Call render interface reset function with (0, 0) to clear state\n4. Reinitialize GDI window with new resolution via FUN_6f891120\n5. Set buffer dimensions based on resolution mode via FUN_6f8925a0\n6. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pUnused (ECX) - void* - Unused parameter, passed via fastcall convention\n  nResolutionMode (EDX) - int - Resolution mode selector:\n    0 = 640x480 (g_nTileProjectOffset=0x280, g_nBufferHeight=0x1e0)\n    3 = Preset (g_nTileProjectOffset=0x540, g_nBufferHeight=700)\n    Other = 800x600 (g_nTileProjectOffset=800, g_nBufferHeight=600)\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating success\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pTileRenderVtable - GDI bitmap handle, deleted and recreated\n  g_pFrameBuffer - Frame buffer pointer, cleared then set by FUN_6f891120\n  g_nTileProjectOffset - Tile projection offset based on resolution\n  g_nBufferHeight - Buffer height based on resolution",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
