      "name": "GetGdiRenderModeFlag",
      "signature": "uint GetGdiRenderModeFlag(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Returns the GDI render mode flag from the global GDI data context structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to g_pGdiDataContext global\n2. Dereference offset +0x14 to get render mode flag value\n3. Return the flag value\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\n- Non-zero: Render mode is active (use palette override path with color 0xC0)\n- Zero: Standard render mode (use default rendering path)\n\nCalled By:\n- DrawCelFrameClipped: Determines if palette override should be applied\n- RenderTileProjectEntries: Selects between two render interface methods\n\nStructure Access:\nOffset 0x14 in GdiDataContext: Render mode flag (uint)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
