      "name": "GetAlphaBlendLevel",
      "signature": "undefined GetAlphaBlendLevel(uint param_1, uint param_2, uint param_3, uint param_4, undefined4 param_5, byte param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Calculates alpha blend level from byte intensity value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read alpha byte from 5th parameter (bAlpha at ESP+0x10)\n2. Compare against threshold bands:\n   - If bAlpha >= 0xC0 (192): return 5 (highest blend)\n   - If bAlpha >= 0x80 (128): return 2 (medium blend)\n   - If bAlpha >= 0x40 (64): return 1 (low blend)\n   - If bAlpha > 0: call fallback with coordinates\n   - If bAlpha == 0: return 0 (no blend)\n3. Return integer blend level for use in rendering\n\nParameters:\n- nX1: X coordinate of first point\n- nY1: Y coordinate of first point\n- nX2: X coordinate of second point\n- nY2: Y coordinate of second point\n- bAlpha: Alpha/intensity byte value (0-255)\n\nReturns:\n- int: Blend level (0, 1, 2, or 5) based on alpha thresholds\n\nNote: Function boundaries appear truncated in Ghidra analysis.\nActual code extends to 0x6f8919e3 (RET 0x10).",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:ceac607c356153cbae631a146fd5334e056c24b29f754a381466382759bf111a",
