      "name": "DrawLineBresenham",
      "signature": "undefined DrawLineBresenham(int param_1, int param_2, int param_3, int param_4, undefined1 param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a line between two points using Bresenham's line algorithm.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate delta X (nX2 - nX1) and delta Y (nY2 - nY1)\n2. Determine step direction signs for X and Y axes\n3. Initialize error accumulator for integer-only calculations\n4. For each step along the major axis:\n   a. Plot pixel at current (x, y) using bColor\n   b. Update error term\n   c. Step in major axis direction\n   d. If error exceeds threshold, step in minor axis direction\n5. Continue until endpoint reached\n\nParameters:\n  nX1 (ECX): Starting X coordinate\n  nY1 (EDX): Starting Y coordinate  \n  nX2 (stack+0x4): Ending X coordinate\n  nY2 (stack+0x8): Ending Y coordinate\n  bColor (stack+0xC): Pixel color value (8-bit palette index)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Pixels drawn directly to frame buffer\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_nTileProjectOffset (0x6f89c05c): Screen width in pixels (stride)\n  g_nBufferHeight (0x6f89c468): Screen height in pixels\n  g_pFrameBuffer (0x6f89c86c): Pointer to screen buffer base\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles all octants via sign flipping of deltas\n  - Bounds checking against screen dimensions before pixel write\n  - Two exit paths: one for steep lines, one for shallow lines\n\nNote: Function body incomplete in Ghidra (single PUSH ECX visible).\nFull function spans 0x6f891a00 to 0x6f891b2b (299 bytes) per hex analysis.\nUses RET 0x10 indicating 16 bytes of stack parameters cleaned by callee.",
