      "name": "ClearFrameBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined ClearFrameBuffer(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Clears the frame buffer memory by zeroing all bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine the effective buffer height\n   - If nUseReducedHeight is non-zero, subtract 0x2f (47) pixels from height\n   - Otherwise use full g_nBufferHeight\n2. Calculate total byte count: dwBufferHeight * g_nTileProjectOffset\n3. Zero memory in DWORD chunks (fast path)\n   - Process dwByteCount / 4 DWORDs\n4. Zero remaining bytes individually (0-3 bytes)\n   - Process dwByteCount % 4 remaining bytes\n\nParameters:\n  nUseReducedHeight (ECX, int) - If non-zero, reduces buffer height by 47 pixels\n                                 Used for partial clears (e.g., excluding UI area)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n  g_nBufferHeight - Source buffer height in pixels\n  g_nTileProjectOffset - Row stride/pitch in bytes\n  g_pFrameBuffer - Pointer to frame buffer memory\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2f (47) - Height reduction for partial clear (likely UI panel height)\n\nPerformance Notes:\n  Uses DWORD-aligned clearing for efficiency, then handles remainder bytes",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
