      "name": "CreateOffscreenDIBSection",
      "signature": "undefined CreateOffscreenDIBSection(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates a Device-Independent Bitmap (DIB) section for GDI offscreen rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert that g_pFrameBuffer is NULL (no existing buffer)\n2. Select resolution dimensions based on nResolutionMode parameter\n3. Log the resolution being opened via QueueLogMessage\n4. Zero-initialize BITMAPINFO structure (0x10a dwords = 0x428 bytes)\n5. Populate BITMAPINFOHEADER fields:\n   - biSize = 0x28 (40 bytes - standard header)\n   - biWidth = g_nTileProjectOffset (screen width)\n   - biHeight = -g_nBufferHeight (negative for top-down DIB)\n   - biPlanes = 1, biBitCount = 8 (8-bit indexed color)\n6. Obtain desktop DC via GetDC(NULL)\n7. Create DIB section via CreateDIBSection, store handle in g_pTileRenderVtable\n8. Release desktop DC\n9. Call render interface initialization with buffer height\n\nParameters:\n  nResolutionMode (ECX): Resolution selector\n    0 = 640x480 (default low resolution)\n    3 = 1344x700 (preset high resolution)\n    other = 800x600 (standard resolution)\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x28 = sizeof(BITMAPINFOHEADER)\n  0x10a = 266 dwords = 1064 bytes BITMAPINFO struct size\n  0x280 = 640, 0x1e0 = 480 (low res)\n  0x320 = 800, 0x258 = 600 (standard)\n  0x540 = 1344, 0x2bc = 700 (high res)\n\nStructure Layout (BITMAPINFOHEADER at stack-0x428):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x00    4     biSize        DWORD   Header size (0x28)\n  0x04    4     biWidth       LONG    Bitmap width in pixels\n  0x08    4     biHeight      LONG    Bitmap height (negative = top-down)\n  0x0C    2     biPlanes      WORD    Color planes (always 1)\n  0x0E    2     biBitCount    WORD    Bits per pixel (8)\n  0x10    4     biCompression DWORD   Compression type (0 = BI_RGB)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
