      "name": "ReleaseSmackerHandle",
      "signature": "undefined ReleaseSmackerHandle(int * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Releases a Smacker video handle and associated resources.\n\nCleans up both the memory pool allocation and the RAD Smacker video handle.\nSafely handles NULL pointers and non-Smacker handle types.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global pool context (g_pSmackerPoolContext) is valid\n2. If valid, call ReleasePoolAllocation to free 0xF0 (240) bytes\n3. Clear the global pool context pointer to NULL\n4. Check if handle type byte equals 's' (0x73 = Smacker type marker)\n5. If Smacker type and pSmackHandle pointer is non-NULL, call SmackClose\n6. Clear the pSmackHandle pointer to NULL\n7. Clear the type byte to 0\n\nParameters:\npHandle - Pointer to SmackerHandle structure passed via ECX register\n          Structure: +0x00 pSmackHandle (void*), +0x04 bType (byte)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Safe to call with NULL pool context - skips pool release\n- Safe to call with non-Smacker type - skips SmackClose\n- Safe to call with NULL pSmackHandle - skips SmackClose\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF0 (240): Size of Smacker pool allocation in bytes\n- 0x73 ('s'): Type marker indicating valid Smacker handle",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:4a8fa3b444a0f9e50aad271fa75df4f0",
