      "name": "SetBufferResolutionMode",
      "signature": "undefined SetBufferResolutionMode(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets the rendering buffer width and X offset based on the resolution mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset X offset (g_nBufferXOffset) to 0\n2. Set buffer width based on resolution mode:\n   - Mode 0: 640 pixels (0x280) - Standard 640x480\n   - Mode 3: 1344 pixels (0x540) - Extended width\n   - Default: 800 pixels (0x320) - 800x600\n\nParameters:\n  nResolutionMode (int, ECX) - Resolution mode selector:\n    0 = 640x480 mode\n    3 = 1344-width mode (likely widescreen)\n    Other = 800x600 mode (default)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Updates global buffer dimension variables\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nBufferWidth (0x6f89c988) - Set to 640, 800, or 1344 based on mode\n  g_nBufferXOffset (0x6f89c98c) - Always set to 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x280 = 640 - Standard VGA width\n  0x320 = 800 - SVGA width  \n  0x540 = 1344 - Extended width for widescreen modes\n\nCalled By:\n  Initialization routines to configure GDI rendering buffer dimensions",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
