      "name": "AcquirePauseRenderLock",
      "signature": "int AcquirePauseRenderLock(void * pRenderContext, byte bRenderMode, int nParam1, int nParam2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Acquires the pause critical section lock for safe render operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_fPauseLockActive (DWORD_6f89c870) is set\n2. If active, return 0 (operation blocked during pause)\n3. Assert g_pcsPause is valid\n4. Enter the pause critical section via EnterCriticalSection\n5. If pRenderContext is valid, delegate to render handler with params\n6. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n  pRenderContext (ECX): Pointer to render context or NULL\n  bRenderMode (DL): Render mode flags byte\n  nParam1 (stack+4): First stack parameter for render operation\n  nParam2 (stack+8): Second stack parameter for render operation\n\nReturns:\n  int - 1 on success, 0 if pause lock is already active\n\nError Handling:\n  Asserts if g_pcsPause is NULL (line 0x111 in gdiCore.cpp)\n\nRelated Functions:\n  LeavePauseCriticalSection - Releases the acquired lock\n\nNotes:\n  Uses __fastcall convention (ECX, DL) plus __stdcall stack cleanup (RET 8).\n  The pause lock prevents concurrent render operations during game pause.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
