      "name": "ZeroFillFrameBuffer",
      "signature": "void ZeroFillFrameBuffer(bool fUseHeightOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears the frame buffer by zeroing all bytes using optimized REP STOSD/STOSB.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test fUseHeightOffset flag in ECX\n2. If true: calculate effective height as (g_nBufferHeight - 47)\n3. If false: use g_nBufferHeight directly as effective height\n4. Multiply effective height by g_nTileProjectOffset to get total byte count\n5. Load g_pFrameBuffer destination pointer into EDI\n6. Zero EAX as fill value\n7. Calculate dword count (total bytes >> 2) and fill with REP STOSD\n8. Calculate remaining bytes (total bytes & 3) and fill with REP STOSB\n9. Return\n\nParameters:\n  fUseHeightOffset (ECX, bool) - If true, subtracts 47 from buffer height before\n                                  calculating total size. Used for partial clears.\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x2F (47) - Height offset adjustment, likely one tile row in pixels\n  0x2      - Right shift for dword count (divide by 4)\n  0x3      - Mask for remaining byte count (modulo 4)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_nBufferHeight    @ 0x6f89c468 - Frame buffer height in pixels\n  g_nTileProjectOffset @ 0x6f89c05c - Buffer stride (bytes per row)\n  g_pFrameBuffer     @ 0x6f89c86c - Pointer to frame buffer memory",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
