      "name": "RenderTileWithOffsetMode",
      "signature": "void RenderTileWithOffsetMode(TileProject * pTileProject, int nColorOrData, int nXPos, int nYPos, int nWidth, int nHeight, int nDepth, int nOffsetMode, int nReserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Renders a tile with optional horizontal offset adjustment based on offset mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate or verify tile project buffer via AllocateTileProjectBuffer\n2. If allocation fails (returns 0), exit immediately\n3. Load X position from stack and subtract 0x50 base offset\n4. Check offset mode parameter:\n   - Mode 0: No offset adjustment\n   - Mode 1: Subtract (g_nTileProjectOffset / 4) from X position\n   - Mode 2: Add (g_nTileProjectOffset / 4) to X position\n5. Call render interface method at g_pRenderInterface+0xC with adjusted coordinates\n\nParameters:\n- pTileProject (ECX): Pointer to TileProject structure for rendering context\n- nColorOrData (EDX): Color or data parameter passed to render method\n- nXPos (stack+0x4): Base X position for rendering\n- nYPos (stack+0x8): Y position passed to render method\n- nWidth (stack+0xC): Width parameter (adjusted by 0x50 offset)\n- nHeight (stack+0x10): Height parameter passed to render method\n- nDepth (stack+0x14): Depth/Z-order parameter\n- nOffsetMode (stack+0x18): Offset mode (0=none, 1=negative, 2=positive)\n- nReserved (stack+0x1C): Reserved parameter\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit if AllocateTileProjectBuffer returns 0 (allocation failure)\n- Offset calculation uses signed division with rounding: (value + 3) >> 2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x50: Base X offset subtracted from position\n- 0xC: Vtable offset for render method in g_pRenderInterface",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
