      "name": "ProcessSmackerVideoFrame",
      "signature": "void ProcessSmackerVideoFrame(SmackerHandle * pSmackCtx)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes a Smacker video frame based on current playback state.\n\nHandles two video states:\n- 's' (0x73): Streaming mode - waits for frame, processes palette, decodes frame\n- 'p' (0x70): Palette copy mode - copies palette-mapped pixels to framebuffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check state byte at pSmackCtx+0x4 for 'p' (0x70) or 's' (0x73)\n2. For 's' state:\n   a. Call SmackWait to sync with video timing\n   b. If palette data exists (offset 0x68), build 256-entry color lookup table\n      by calling FindClosestColorMatch for each RGB triplet in Smack palette\n   c. Call SmackDoFrame to decode current frame\n   d. If at last frame (current == total), call SmackClose\n3. For 'p' state:\n   Copy palette-mapped pixels from source to destination framebuffer\n   using lookup table at 0x6f89c880 for palette translation\n4. Apply calculated screen offset (nYOffset * stride + nXOffset)\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackCtx (ECX): SmackerHandle* - Video playback context containing:\n    +0x00: pSmack - Pointer to RAD Smacker structure\n    +0x04: bState - State byte ('s'=stream, 'p'=palette copy)\n    +0x08: nXOffset - Horizontal screen offset\n    +0x0C: nYOffset - Vertical screen offset\n\nReturns:\n  void - Frame is processed in place\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x70 ('p'): Palette copy state\n  0x73 ('s'): Streaming/decode state\n  0x100: Palette entry count (256 colors)\n  0x3C: Vertical offset for palette mode (60 pixels)\n  0x1D4: Bytes per scanline in palette mode (468 pixels)\n\nStructure Layout (RAD Smack structure at pSmack):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  0x04    4     dwWidth         Video width in pixels\n  0x08    4     dwHeight        Video height in pixels\n  0x0C    4     dwTotalFrames   Total frame count\n  0x68    4     dwPaletteFlag   Non-zero if palette needs processing\n  0x6D    768   abPalette       RGB palette data (256 * 3 bytes)\n  0x374   4     dwCurrentFrame  Current frame number\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  0x6f89c05c: dwScreenStride - Screen buffer stride\n  0x6f89c86c: pScreenBuffer - Destination screen buffer\n  0x6f89c870: dwPauseFlag - Video pause state\n  0x6f89c880: abPaletteMap - 256-byte palette lookup table\n  0x6f89c980: pSourceBuffer - Source video buffer\n  0x6f89c984: dwPaletteReady - Palette processing complete flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:6f3bc6065e73f2d742a6517c835f292c411ba539514e5d83b203f1ac3eeee3e3",
