      "name": "RefreshViewportAtCoordinates",
      "signature": "void RefreshViewportAtCoordinates(int nX, int nY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Validates viewport coordinates and refreshes the scroll region at the specified position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nX is within valid buffer width range (0 < nX < g_nTileProjectOffset - 80)\n2. Validate nY is within valid buffer height range (0 < nY < g_nBufferHeight - 80)\n3. If both coordinates valid, calculate pixel offset and call RefreshViewportScrollRegion\n4. If nX invalid, assert with \"nX > 0 && nX < gnBufferWidth - 80\" and report error\n5. If nY invalid, assert with \"nY > 0 && nY < gnBufferHeight - 80\" and report error\n\nParameters:\n- nX (int, ECX): X coordinate in the viewport buffer, must be > 0 and < buffer width - 80\n- nY (int, EDX): Y coordinate in the viewport buffer, must be > 0 and < buffer height - 80\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, but early returns on validation success\n\nError Handling:\n- Calls FogAssert with assertion expression and source file location on validation failure\n- Calls ReportError(-1) after assertion failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x50 (80): Margin/border size subtracted from buffer dimensions for valid coordinate range\n- 0x1a8 (424): Line number for X coordinate assertion\n- 0x1a9 (425): Line number for Y coordinate assertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:4dadf83635478390bad8baa2a64f29e5",
