      "name": "DrawClippedCelFrame",
      "signature": "undefined DrawClippedCelFrame(uint * param_1, int param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Draws a CEL frame clipped to a specified rectangle boundary.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load or retrieve the CEL frame data from cache\n2. Get CelFileInfo pointer and extract table index and mode value\n3. Calculate horizontal clip bounds (nClipLeft, nClipRight) clamped to g_nTileProjectOffset\n4. Early exit if frame completely outside horizontal clip region\n5. Get CEL height and check if frame intersects vertical clip region\n6. Calculate vertical clip bounds (nClipTop, nClipBottom) clamped to g_nBufferHeight\n7. Compute bottom edge position (nBottomEdge = celWidth + nScreenX)\n8. Calculate nYSkipRows (rows to skip from top) based on clip bottom\n9. Calculate nRowCount (visible rows to render) based on clip bounds\n10. Assert nRowCount > 0 or report fatal error\n11. Select output buffer from g_pOutputBufferTable based on buffer mode (0-6)\n12. Call DecodeCelFrame with clipped parameters to render visible portion\n\nParameters:\n    pCelFrameData (ECX): Pointer to CEL frame data structure containing frame info\n    pnScreenY (EDX): Pointer to screen Y coordinate for rendering\n    nScreenX (stack): Screen X coordinate for rendering position\n    pClipRect (stack): Pointer to clip rectangle as 4 uints [left, right, top, bottom]\n\nReturns:\n    void - Renders directly to selected output buffer\n\nClip Rectangle Structure (pClipRect):\n    Offset  Size  Field   Description\n    0x00    4     left    Left clip boundary (clamped to 0 if negative)\n    0x04    4     right   Right clip boundary (clamped to g_nTileProjectOffset)\n    0x08    4     top     Top clip boundary (clamped to 0 if negative)\n    0x0C    4     bottom  Bottom clip boundary (clamped to g_nBufferHeight)\n\nOutput Buffer Modes (switch on pClipRect[1] after clamping):\n    0: g_pOutputBufferTable[2] (offset +0x08)\n    1: g_pOutputBufferTable[1] (offset +0x04)\n    2: g_pOutputBufferTable[0] (offset +0x00)\n    3: g_pOutputBufferTable[65] (offset +0x104)\n    4: g_pOutputBufferTable[66] (offset +0x108)\n    6: g_pOutputBufferTable[67] (offset +0x10C)\n    default: NULL\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - Returns early if LoadOrRetrieveCelFrameData fails\n    - Returns early if frame completely outside clip region\n    - Asserts and calls ReportError(-1) if calculated row count <= 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.09",
