      "name": "ReportSecurityError",
      "signature": "void ReportSecurityError(int errorType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Displays a security error dialog and terminates the process. Handles buffer overflow and unknown security failures by showing a message box with the module name and error details. If a custom security handler is registered, calls it; otherwise exits with code 3.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize stack cookie XOR value for buffer overflow protection\n2. Check if custom security handler (DAT_6f87bf6c) is registered\n3. If handler exists, call it with parameters and mark completion\n4. If no handler, determine error type (buffer overrun vs unknown)\n5. Get module file name using GetModuleFileNameA\n6. If module name retrieval fails, use fallback name \"<program_name_unknown>\"\n7. Calculate message buffer space and truncate module path if needed (max 60 chars)\n8. Allocate aligned stack buffer for error message construction\n9. Build error message by concatenating:\n   - Error type string (buffer overrun or unknown security failure)\n   - Module file path\n   - Error description based on type\n10. Display message box with full error message\n11. Exit process with code 3\n\nParameters:\n- errorType: Error classification code (1 = buffer overrun, other = unknown security failure)\n\nReturns:\n- void (function terminates process, never returns)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- GetModuleFileNameA failure triggers fallback to \"<program_name_unknown>\"\n- Message path truncation: If (strlen(modulePath) + 11) > 60, path is truncated with \"...\"\n- Stack allocation uses alignment: (strlen + ESI + 12 + 3) & 0xfffffffc for 4-byte boundary\n- Buffer overflow detection uses XOR stack cookie at offset -0x1c",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:6829c7e2ecf5617d1af04a2d6d84fcdc",
