      "name": "GetGameConfigValue",
      "signature": "uint GetGameConfigValue(uint selectorIndex, uint * pOutputValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves game configuration values from indexed lookup table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate selector index against maximum (6)\n2. Load base offset from DAT_6f87bb80 indexed by selectorIndex\n3. Write offset value to output parameter\n4. Perform switch dispatch on selectorIndex (0-6)\n5. Load corresponding config value from DAT_6f87c550 with calculated offset\n6. Return config value in EAX, or 0 if selector invalid\n\nParameters:\nselectorIndex: Selector index (0-6) determining which config offset to retrieve\npOutputValue: Pointer to uint output receiving base offset from DAT_6f87bb80\n\nReturns:\nuint value from DAT_6f87c550 at calculated offset, or 0 if selectorIndex > 6\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- selectorIndex must be 0-6; values > 6 return 0\n- Case 5 falls through to default (returns 0)\n- Offsets used: case 0=+0x8, case 1=+0x4, case 2=+0x0, case 3=+0x104, case 4=+0x108, case 6=+0x10c\n\nStructure Layout:\nConfig Table (DAT_6f87c550):\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type        Description\n+0x00   4     value_0         uint        Config value for selector 2\n+0x04   4     value_1         uint        Config value for selector 1\n+0x08   4     value_2         uint        Config value for selector 0\n+0x104  4     value_3         uint        Config value for selector 3\n+0x108  4     value_4         uint        Config value for selector 4\n+0x10c  4     value_6         uint        Config value for selector 6",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
