      "name": "InitializePaletteAndApplyToDevice",
      "signature": "void InitializePaletteAndApplyToDevice(PALETTEENTRY * pPaletteData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game palette and applies it to the graphics device.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy source palette data byte-by-byte to internal palette buffer (0x6f87c150) with 0x400 byte capacity\n2. Read 256 PALETTEENTRY structures from input parameter into the buffer\n3. Call SetPaletteEntries Windows API to apply palette to graphics device handle\n4. Copy all 256 palette entries from input to backup buffer at 0x6f87c680\n\nParameters:\n- pPaletteData (PALETTEENTRY *): Pointer to array of 256 PALETTEENTRY structures to apply. Each structure contains RGB color data for one palette entry (peRed, peGreen, peBlue, peFlags).\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Palette buffer at 0x6f87c150 is 0x400 bytes (1024 bytes = 256 * 4 bytes per entry)\n- Backup buffer at 0x6f87c680 stores full copy of applied palette\n- SetPaletteEntries call uses parameters: hdc=DAT_6f87ca84, iStart=0, nEntries=0x100 (256)\n- Assumes pPaletteData is valid and points to at least 256 PALETTEENTRY entries\n\nStructure Layout:\nPALETTEENTRY structure (4 bytes per entry):\nOffset  Size  Field Name  Type     Description\n0       1     peRed       BYTE     Red component (0-255)\n1       1     peGreen     BYTE     Green component (0-255)\n2       1     peBlue      BYTE     Blue component (0-255)\n3       1     peFlags     BYTE     Palette entry flags",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d023401588809fbebb1e56aa046edc27",
