      "signature": "void CloseSmackHandle(SmackHandle * pSmackHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Closes a Smack video codec handle and clears initialization state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if module initialization flag (DAT_6f87c148) is non-zero\n2. If set, call InitializeModule with parameters 0xf0 and 0 to reinitialize\n3. Clear the initialization flag to 0\n4. Check if pSmackHandle->type equals 's' (0x73) and handle is non-null\n5. If both conditions are true, call SmackClose with the handle value\n6. Clear the handle to 0\n7. Clear the type byte to 0\n\nParameters:\n  pSmackHandle (SmackHandle*) - Pointer to Smack handle structure containing:\n    hHandle (offset 0x0) - Handle value for SmackClose function\n    type (offset 0x4) - Type identifier byte (0x73='s' for Smack resources)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If DAT_6f87c148 is non-zero, module reinitialization occurs before cleanup\n  - Handle is only closed if type byte is exactly 0x73\n  - Both handle and type byte are cleared to 0 on successful close\n  - Function is called via __fastcall with handle in ECX register",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ae5884d93175085a985e38b41719369c",
